# Rapspect - line endings and binary files
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# Every `git add` on Windows printed a warning about LF being replaced by CRLF.
# The warning was harmless, but it meant line endings depended on whoever cloned
# the repository. Normalising them here makes a diff show only real changes.

# Store text with LF in the repository and check it out with LF everywhere.
# Chrome, Node and PowerShell all read LF without complaint, so there is no
# reason to keep a platform split.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts keep CRLF. Some older Windows PowerShell hosts are still
# fussy about this, and a build tool is not worth debugging over line endings.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch these. Line ending conversion would corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf

# Keep generated icons and the source logo out of diff output. They are binary,
# so a diff is unreadable noise that hides the real changes in a pull request.
assets/icons/*.png -diff
assets/branding/*.png -diff
assets/Rapspect.jpg -diff
assets/Rapspect.jpeg -diff
Rapspect.jpg -diff
